            "body": "Rebased onto current main (e624174f) to resolve the conflict: main dropped the `cuda-tile` pin next to this line, so the change is still the same two lines in `python/pyproject.toml`.\n\nThe mismatch is still present on main. Resolving main's dependencies for Linux x86_64 / Python 3.12 gives nvcc/CRT/NVVM 13.4.92 and CCCL 13.3 next to torch 2.14.1's CUDA 13.0.96 runtime, because `humming-kernels[cu13]==0.1.18` still leaves `nvidia-cuda-nvcc` and `nvidia-cuda-cccl` unpinned. With this change the resolution succeeds and selects nvcc/CRT/NVVM 13.0.88 and CCCL 13.0.85, matching torch's own `cuda-toolkit==13.0.3` requirement.\n\n#46418 / #46420 (libcudart link layout of the pip toolkit) build on this pin, and #46803 refers to it as well.\n\n@Fridge003 @ispobock @merrymercy could one of you add the `run-ci` label when you have a moment? The current failures are all `Missing required label 'run-ci'` from the PR gate.\n",
