  "files": [
    {
      "additions": 2,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/0ec1c2c58ab17355b9daefcd9146e711dd3cf6c8/python%2Fpyproject.toml",
      "changes": 2,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/python%2Fpyproject.toml?ref=0ec1c2c58ab17355b9daefcd9146e711dd3cf6c8",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "python/pyproject.toml",
      "patch": "@@ -30,6 +30,8 @@ dependencies = [\n   \"build\",\n   \"compressed-tensors==0.18.0\",\n   \"cuda-python>=13.0\",\n+  # Match the JIT compiler/headers to torch's CUDA 13.0 runtime.\n+  \"cuda-toolkit[nvcc,nvvm,cccl]==13.0.3\",\n   \"datasets\",\n   \"decord2 ; sys_platform == 'linux' and (platform_machine == 'aarch64' or platform_machine == 'arm64' or platform_machine == 'armv7l')\",\n   \"deepseek-recipe==0.2.0 ; (sys_platform == 'linux' and (platform_machine == 'x86_64' or platform_machine == 'aarch64')) or sys_platform == 'darwin'\",",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/raw/0ec1c2c58ab17355b9daefcd9146e711dd3cf6c8/python%2Fpyproject.toml",
      "sha": "93f79d18006ed6d76d53274a1c5abf8c90c63f06",
      "status": "modified"
    }
  ],
  "inline_comments": [],
  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "Rebased onto current main (e624174f) to resolve the conflict: main dropped the `cuda-tile` pin next to this line, so the change is still the same two lines in `python/pyproject.toml`.\n\nThe mismatch is still present on main. Resolving main's dependencies for Linux x86_64 / Python 3.12 gives nvcc/CRT/NVVM 13.4.92 and CCCL 13.3 next to torch 2.14.1's CUDA 13.0.96 runtime, because `humming-kernels[cu13]==0.1.18` still leaves `nvidia-cuda-nvcc` and `nvidia-cuda-cccl` unpinned. With this change the resolution succeeds and selects nvcc/CRT/NVVM 13.0.88 and CCCL 13.0.85, matching torch's own `cuda-toolkit==13.0.3` requirement.\n\n#46418 / #46420 (libcudart link layout of the pip toolkit) build on this pin, and #46803 refers to it as well.\n\n@Fridge003 @ispobock @merrymercy could one of you add the `run-ci` label when you have a moment? The current failures are all `Missing required label 'run-ci'` from the PR gate.\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-31T18:37:44Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/43591#issuecomment-6547542089",
      "id": 6547542089,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-31T18:37:44Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "Winterslife"
      }
    }
